<title>SRI LANKA: Weather - Widespread showers seen over Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather - Widespread showers seen over Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's meteorological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   40.4</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    19.0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  19.5</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 15.2</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     13.4</p>
<p>    Norton		   49.6</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     2.5</p>
<p>    Victoria		 16.1</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	   16.0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		  18.0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  2.3</p>
<p>The department forecast widespread showers over the island. It said seas off the southeast coast will be rough with occasional thundershowers and fairly strong winds.</p>
</text>
